1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,920
Here's something cool!

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:06,560
c, k, and ck all make the same /k/ sound!

3
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:08,320
Three spellings...

4
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:09,680
one sound!

5
00:00:10,140 --> 00:00:12,480
Let's see how!

6
00:00:12,540 --> 00:00:14,480
Listen: c-at...

7
00:00:16,060 --> 00:00:16,820
k-ite...

8
00:00:18,300 --> 00:00:19,440
du-ck.

9
00:00:20,250 --> 00:00:21,940
/k/, /k/, /k/!

10
00:00:22,940 --> 00:00:25,440
Same sound, three different spellings.

11
00:00:26,820 --> 00:00:27,770
So how do we choose?

12
00:00:28,960 --> 00:00:31,580
It depends on where the sound is in the word!

13
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:34,940
We use c most of the time.

14
00:00:35,440 --> 00:00:44,760
At the start of a word, before a, o, or u, we use c — c-at, c-ot, c-up!

15
00:00:46,120 --> 00:00:48,840
But there's one special rule!

16
00:00:48,840 --> 00:00:53,940
Before e and i, c says /s/, like in city.

17
00:00:54,920 --> 00:01:07,620
So when we hear /k/ instead of /s/, before e or i, we write k — k-ey, k-it, k-ing!

18
00:01:09,220 --> 00:01:19,080
And at the end of a word, right after one short vowel, we use ck — two letters, but just one /k/ sound!

19
00:01:19,080 --> 00:01:23,960
du-ck, ro-ck, ki-ck!

20
00:01:25,400 --> 00:01:26,700
Let's try some words!

21
00:01:27,900 --> 00:01:32,540
c: cat, cup, cot.

22
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:37,840
k: key, kit, king.

23
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:43,480
ck: duck, rock, kick!

24
00:01:45,240 --> 00:01:46,520
Now it's your turn!

25
00:01:47,220 --> 00:01:48,260
How do we spell duck?

26
00:01:49,340 --> 00:01:52,200
c, k, or ck?

27
00:01:54,060 --> 00:01:57,900
It's ck — because there's a short vowel right before it!

28
00:01:59,420 --> 00:02:02,740
Remember: c before a, o, and u...

29
00:02:03,560 --> 00:02:05,520
k before e and i...

30
00:02:06,220 --> 00:02:09,420
and ck after a short vowel at the end.

31
00:02:10,120 --> 00:02:11,420
Easy trick, right?

32
00:02:12,720 --> 00:02:18,910
